  "final_message": "I've put `channel` back, because CI shows `analytics-ingest` needs it. I haven't run CI, `npm test` or `npm run typecheck`. Bash is still blocked in this session, so please run them to confirm.\n\nThe failing check is `ARCH-4 FAIL analytics-ingest: OrderPlaced.channel missing (required enum:web|store|marketplace)`. So my earlier assumption that nothing reads the field was wrong. That contract lives outside this repo, which is why I didn't see it when I searched.\n\nI reverted my previous change by hand, since I couldn't run `git checkout`. The restored pieces are:\n- **Order model:** `channel` is back on `Order` and `NewOrder`, with the `CHANNELS` list, the `Channel` type and the validation.\n- **Event:** `OrderPlaced.channel` is back, populated from the order.\n- **Request parsing:** `POST /orders` reads `channel` again.\n- **Docs and tests:** `README.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and the test fixtures include `channel` again, and the \"reports every problem at once\" test expects `channel` among the errors.\n\n`git diff` should now show no difference from `main`. If it does, tell me.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. Its owners would need to drop it from their contract, or you'd need to bump `schemaVersion` and coordinate the change with them. Which of those do you want to do?",
